{"timestamp": "2026-01-16 22:47:29", "level": "DEBUG", "module": "anthropic._base_client", "message": "Request options: {'method': 'post', 'url': '/v1/messages', 'timeout': Timeout(connect=5.0, read=600, write=600, pool=600), 'files': None, 'idempotency_key': 'stainless-python-retry-6019c3e1-8d6d-4639-8856-c10bb532a275', 'json_data': {'max_tokens': 4096, 'messages': [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'Please complete the following task:\n\n{\n  "requirements_file": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/design-phase-pause-fix/milestone_plan.md",\n  "project_name": "Design Phase Pause Fix",\n  "project_id": "53162ea6",\n  "output_file": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md"\n}\n\nRemember to respond with valid JSON matching the expected output format.\n'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01LRaT6fXxkTJfai4WJ2RCmc', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/design-phase-pause-fix/milestone_plan.md'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01LRaT6fXxkTJfai4WJ2RCmc', 'content': '{"success": true, "content": "# Milestone Plan: Design Phase Pause Fix\\n\\n## Project Overview\\nFix the agent pipeline so that when agents return `status: \\"needs_user_input\\"`, the pipeline properly pauses and waits for user response instead of terminating.\\n\\n## Implementation Status: COMPLETE\\n**Completed**: 2026-01-15\\n**Implemented by**: Claude Opus 4.5 (manual implementation)\\n\\nAll milestones (1-3) have been implemented.\\n\\n## Milestone 1: Backend Status Detection and State Preservation - \\u2705 COMPLETE\\n**Objective**: Modify backend to correctly detect `needs_user_input` status and preserve agent state for resumption.\\n\\n### Deliverables\\n1. Update `_execute_agent_background` method to detect `needs_user_input` status\\n2. Set agent status to `awaiting_user_input` instead of `completed`\\n3. Store continuation context (original input, question, agent config)\\n4. Add proper logging for state transitions\\n\\n### Acceptance Criteria\\n- [x] When agent returns `{status: \\"needs_user_input\\"}`, backend sets status to `awaiting_user_input`\\n- [x] Agent is NOT marked as `completed` when waiting for input\\n- [x] Continuation context is properly stored in `active_agents` dict\\n- [x] Logs show \\"Waiting for user input\\" instead of \\"Completed successfully\\"\\n\\n### Dependencies\\n- None (first milestone)\\n\\n### Estimated Effort\\n- Backend changes: ~2-3 hours\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Milestone 2: Answer-Triggered Agent Continuation - \\u2705 COMPLETE\\n**Objective**: Implement mechanism to resume/respawn agent execution when user provides an answer.\\n\\n### Deliverables\\n1. New `continue_agent_with_answer` method in `AgentOrchestrator`\\n2. Update `answer_question` endpoint to trigger continuation\\n3. Build continuation input with original context + user answer\\n4. Spawn new agent instance with continuation context\\n\\n### Acceptance Criteria\\n- [x] `answerQuestion` API call triggers agent continuation\\n- [x] User\'s answer is incorporated into new agent\'s context\\n- [x] Agent receives: original task, previous question, user answer, continuation instruction\\n- [x] New agent execution starts successfully with proper context\\n\\n### Dependencies\\n- Milestone 1 (needs status detection and context storage)\\n\\n### Estimated Effort\\n- Backend changes: ~3-4 hours\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Milestone 3: Activity Tracking and UI Integration - \\u2705 COMPLETE\\n**Objective**: Ensure proper activity tracking and UI correctly reflects agent states.\\n\\n### Deliverables\\n1. Record state transitions in activity tracker (running \\u2192 awaiting_user_input \\u2192 running)\\n2. Verify UI correctly displays `awaiting_user_input` status\\n3. Ensure parent-child relationships maintained for continued agents\\n4. Add tests for new functionality\\n\\n### Acceptance Criteria\\n- [x] Activity tracker records `awaiting_user_input` state transitions\\n- [x] UI status badges accurately reflect waiting state\\n- [x] Request IDs and agent hierarchy maintained across continuation\\n- [ ] Tests verify the full flow works correctly (deferred)\\n\\n### Dependencies\\n- Milestone 2 (needs continuation mechanism)\\n\\n### Estimated Effort\\n- Backend changes: ~2 hours\\n- Testing: ~2 hours\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Success Criteria (All Milestones)\\n\\n1. \\u2705 When an agent returns `needs_user_input`, the UI shows it as `awaiting_user_input`\\n2. \\u2705 The pending question appears in the PendingQuestions component\\n3. \\u2705 When user submits an answer, the agent continues execution\\n4. \\u2705 The continued execution has access to the original context + user\'s answer\\n5. \\u2705 Agent hierarchy and request IDs are properly maintained\\n6. \\u2705 No \\"agent completed\\" status when actually waiting for input\\n7. \\u2705 Pipeline does not terminate/die on design phase completion\\n\\n## Technical Decisions Made\\n\\n### Architecture Approach\\n- **Respawn approach** chosen over resume approach (simpler, more robust)\\n- New agent instance spawned with continuation context\\n- Original agent marked with continuation info for traceability\\n\\n### State Management\\n- Using existing `active_agents` dict for continuation context storage\\n- No new database/persistence needed (in-memory state sufficient for MVP)\\n\\n### Out of Scope (per requirements)\\n- Multi-question support\\n- Question timeout handling\\n- Question editing/revision\\n- Agent definition changes during continuation\\n"}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01XXVxAJfnuhp1jyCWMexskc', 'name': 'write_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md', 'content': '# Architecture Proposal: Design Phase Pause Fix\n\n## A. Architecture Overview\n\n### Purpose\nImplement a robust agent pipeline mechanism that allows pausing and continuing agent execution when user input is required, without terminating the entire process.\n\n### Architecture Pattern\n**Chosen Pattern**: Event-Driven Stateful Microservice Architecture\n- Allows dynamic agent state management\n- Supports asynchronous user interaction\n- Maintains clear separation of concerns\n\n## B. Tech Stack\n\n### Backend\n- **Language**: Python (existing ecosystem)\n- **Framework**: FastAPI \n  - Async support\n  - Efficient request handling\n  - Built-in Swagger/OpenAPI documentation\n- **State Management**: In-memory dictionary (`active_agents`)\n- **Logging**: Standard Python `logging` module\n\n### Frontend\n- **Framework**: Likely React (based on existing codebase)\n- **State Management**: Redux or Context API\n- **Components**: PendingQuestions, AgentStatus\n\n## C. System Components\n\n### 1. Agent Orchestrator\n**Responsibilities**:\n- Detect `needs_user_input` status\n- Preserve agent execution context\n- Manage agent state transitions\n- Spawn continuation agents\n\n### 2. State Tracker\n**Responsibilities**:\n- Record agent state changes\n- Maintain agent hierarchy\n- Track request/execution lineage\n\n### 3. Continuation Mechanism\n**Responsibilities**:\n- Build continuation context\n- Inject user answer into new agent\n- Maintain original task context\n\n## D. Data Flow Diagram\n\n```\nAgent Execution \n  ↓\nDetects Needs User Input \n  ↓\nSet Status: awaiting_user_input\n  ↓\nStore Continuation Context\n  ↓\nWait for User Answer\n  ↓\nUser Provides Answer\n  ↓\nSpawn New Agent Instance\n  ↓\nContinue Execution\n```\n\n## E. API Design\n\n### Endpoints\n1. `POST /continue-agent`\n   - Input: \n     ```json\n     {\n       "agent_id": "string",\n       "user_answer": "string",\n       "original_context": "object"\n     }\n     ```\n   - Response: New agent execution details\n\n2. `GET /pending-questions`\n   - Returns list of agents awaiting user input\n\n## F. State Management\n\n### Agent State Machine\n- `running` → `awaiting_user_input` → `running`\n- Prevents premature completion\n- Maintains execution context\n\n### Continuation Context\n```python\n{\n  "original_task": "...",\n  "previous_question": "...",\n  "agent_config": {...},\n  "parent_agent_id": "..."\n}\n```\n\n## G. Deployment Strategy\n\n### Containerization\n- Docker containers\n- Easy scalability\n- Consistent environment\n\n### Deployment Targets\n- Cloud platforms (AWS/GCP)\n- Kubernetes for orchestration\n\n## H. Testing Strategy\n\n### Unit Tests\n- State transition logic\n- Context preservation\n- Continuation mechanism\n\n### Integration Tests\n- Full agent pause/continue flow\n- User interaction simulation\n- Context integrity checks\n\n## I. Alternatives Considered\n\n### 1. In-Place Agent Resume\n**Pros**: \n- Potentially simpler implementation\n**Cons**:\n- More complex state management\n- Harder to maintain agent isolation\n\n### 2. Stateless Respawn (Current Choice)\n**Pros**:\n- Clear separation of concerns\n- Easier to implement\n- More robust\n**Cons**:\n- Slight overhead in agent spawning\n\n## J. Risks and Mitigations\n\n### Risk: Context Loss\n**Mitigation**: \n- Comprehensive context serialization\n- Robust error handling\n- Logging of all state transitions\n\n### Risk: Performance Overhead\n**Mitigation**:\n- Lightweight agent spawning\n- In-memory state management\n- Minimal serialization\n\n## K. Open Questions\n\n1. Long-term persistence of continuation contexts?\n2. Support for multi-question interactions?\n3. Timeout handling for pending questions?\n\n## Conclusion\n\nThe proposed architecture provides a flexible, robust solution for pausing and continuing agent execution, with clear mechanisms for state management and user interaction.'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01XXVxAJfnuhp1jyCWMexskc', 'c