e 1: Performance Benchmarking (Current Model)\n**Objective**: Establish baseline performance metrics for current haiku model\n**Timeline**: 1-2 hours\n**Deliverables**:\n- Current model performance analysis\n- Test execution metrics\n- Success rate documentation\n- Baseline report\n\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\n- Performance metrics documented for current model\n- Baseline success rate established\n- Test coverage analysis complete\n- Current workflow documented\n\n**Dependencies**: None\n\n### Milestone 2: Model Migration Implementation\n**Objective**: Migrate TDD Coordinator to use sonnet model\n**Timeline**: 2-3 hours\n**Deliverables**:\n- Updated TDD Coordinator configuration\n- Model transition implementation\n- Configuration validation\n- Migration documentation\n\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\n- TDD Coordinator successfully using sonnet model\n- All existing functionality preserved\n- Configuration properly updated\n- No breaking changes introduced\n\n**Dependencies**: Milestone 1 complete\n\n### Milestone 3: Performance Validation & Comparison\n**Objective**: Validate performance improvements and compare with baseline\n**Timeline**: 2-3 hours\n**Deliverables**:\n- New model performance metrics\n- Comparative analysis report\n- Success rate validation\n- Final recommendation\n\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\n- Performance improvement of 50% or more achieved\n- No regression in test coverage\n- Comparative analysis documented\n- Validation criteria met\n\n**Dependencies**: Milestone 2 complete\n\n## Success Criteria\n- Performance improvement of 50% or more\n- No regression in existing test coverage\n- Minimal disruption to current workflow\n- Complete documentation of changes and results\n\n## Risk Mitigation\n- Maintain backup of current configuration\n- Incremental testing approach\n- Rollback plan if performance degrades\n- Documentation of all changes for audit trail'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01HocmHBrnYi5NJmDHLip9JC', 'content': '{"success": true, "message": "File written successfully to /Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan.md (backup: /Users/mattbillock/.ensemble/backups/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan_20260116_224247.md)", "backup_path": "/Users/mattbillock/.ensemble/backups/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan_20260116_224247.md", "was_overwrite": true}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01GTajbDperHF1np3Td2JBUB', 'name': 'spawn_agent', 'input': {'agent_type': 'leadership/system_architect', 'input_data': {'requirements_file': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/tdd_coordinator_model_validation_requirements.md', 'project_context': 'TDD Coordinator Model Update - migrating from claude-3-5-haiku-20241022 to claude-sonnet-4-5-20250929', 'output_file': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md'}}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01GTajbDperHF1np3Td2JBUB', 'content': '{"success": true, "result": {"status": "success", "architecture_file": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md", "message": "Comprehensive architecture proposal for TDD Coordinator Model Validation, focusing on systematic performance comparison between Claude models with minimal system disruption", "key_decisions": ["Use Python for model validation framework", "Implement lightweight comparative analysis approach", "Focus on statistically significant performance metrics", "Maintain minimal changes to existing system"], "self_analysis": "The architecture successfully addresses the experimental validation requirements by providing a scientifically rigorous framework for comparing AI models in TDD scenarios. The modular design enables clear separation of concerns while maintaining flexibility for future model comparisons."}}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_012P3kveman6TgUqAGst3uNN', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_012P3kveman6TgUqAGst3uNN', 'content': '{"success": true, "content": "# TDD Coordinator Model Validation Architecture Proposal\\n\\n## A) Architecture Overview\\nA focused, lightweight architecture to validate AI model performance improvements with minimal system disruption. The primary goal is to create a comparative validation framework that can systematically measure and compare the performance of two AI models in test-driven development scenarios.\\n\\n## B) Tech Stack\\n- **Language**: Python 3.9+\\n- **AI Integration**: Anthropic Claude API\\n- **Performance Tracking**: \\n  - Pandas for data analysis\\n  - Matplotlib/Seaborn for visualization\\n- **Validation Framework**: \\n  - pytest for testing infrastructure\\n  - Custom validation modules\\n\\n### Rationale\\n- Python chosen for its strong data analysis and AI integration capabilities\\n- Lightweight stack to minimize overhead and maintain focus on performance validation\\n- Pandas/Matplotlib provide robust tools for statistical analysis and visualization\\n\\n## C) System Components\\n1. **Model Comparison Manager**\\n   - Manages model switching and performance tracking\\n   - Implements benchmark and comparison logic\\n   - Handles API interactions with Claude models\\n\\n2. **Performance Metrics Collector**\\n   - Captures detailed performance metrics\\n   - Tracks success rates, generation times, test coverage\\n   - Generates comparative reports\\n\\n3. **Validation Executor**\\n   - Runs systematic performance tests\\n   - Applies consistent test scenarios across both models\\n   - Ensures statistically significant sample size\\n\\n## D) File/Directory Structure\\n```\\ntdd_model_validation/\\n\\u2502\\n\\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 src/\\n\\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 model_manager.py        # Model switching and API interaction\\n\\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 metrics_collector.py    # Performance tracking\\n\\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 validation_executor.py  # Test execution framework\\n\\u2502   \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 utils/                  # Utility modules\\n\\u2502\\n\\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 tests/                      # Validation test cases\\n\\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 benchmark_tests.py\\n\\u2502   \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 comparative_tests.py\\n\\u2502\\n\\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 results/                    # Output metrics and reports\\n\\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 raw_metrics/\\n\\u2502   \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 reports/\\n\\u2502\\n\\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 config.yaml                 # Configuration settings\\n```\\n\\n## E) Data Model\\n- Performance Metrics Schema:\\n  ```python\\n  {\\n    \\"model_name\\": str,\\n    \\"test_scenario\\": str,\\n    \\"success_rate\\": float,\\n    \\"generation_time\\": float,\\n    \\"coverage_percentage\\": float\\n  }\\n  ```\\n\\n## F) Validation Strategy\\n1. **Benchmark Current Model**\\n   - Run comprehensive test suite with current model\\n   - Capture baseline metrics\\n   - Establish statistical baseline\\n\\n2. **Model Migration**\\n   - Implement minimal changes to switch between models\\n   - Ensure identical test scenarios and environments\\n\\n3. **Comparative Analysis**\\n   - Run identical test scenarios on new model\\n   - Compare performance metrics\\n   - Statistical significance testing\\n\\n## G) Deployment Considerations\\n- Local execution for initial validation\\n- Containerization with Docker for consistent environment\\n- Potential future CI/CD integration for automated comparisons\\n\\n## H) Risks and Mitigations\\n1. **Risk**: Inconsistent test scenarios\\n   - **Mitigation**: Strict test scenario standardization\\n   - **Approach**: Create reproducible, deterministic test cases\\n\\n2. **Risk**: API rate limits or inconsistencies\\n   - **Mitigation**: Implement robust error handling\\n   - **Approach**: Exponential backoff, comprehensive logging\\n\\n## I) Open Questions\\n- Exact number of test scenarios needed for statistical significance\\n- Specific performance improvement metrics beyond success rate\\n\\n## J) Alternatives Considered\\n- Full system rewrite (Rejected - out of scope)\\n- More complex multi-model comparison framework (Rejected - over-engineering)\\n\\n## K) Success Criteria\\n- 50% performance improvement verification\\n- Minimal system disruption\\n- Reproducible, statistically significant results"}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01A7CcdynTfPXiG3DdKDn6WH', 'name': 'spawn_agent', 'input': {'agent_type': 'coordinators/backend_coordinator', 'input_data': {'milestone': 'Performance Benchmarking - Establish baseline performance metrics for current haiku model', 'architecture': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md', 'requirements': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/tdd_coordinator_model_validation_requirements.md', 'output_file': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/backend_tasks_m1.md'}}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01A7CcdynTfPXiG3DdKDn6WH', 'content': '{"success": true, "result": {"status": "success", "tasks_identified": 9, "task_file": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/backend_tasks_m1.md", "dependencies": ["Task 1 \\u2192 Task 2 \\u2192 Task 3 \\u2192 Task 7", "Task 1 \\u2192 Task 9", "Task 2 \\u2192 Task 4 \\u2192 Task 6", "Task 2 \\u2192 Task 4 \\u2192 Task 7", "Task 4 \\u2192 Task 8", "Task 5 (independent)"], "message": "Successfully analyzed performance benchmarkin