xecutive_director", "note": "Project \'Logs Agents Tab Implementation\' created", "category": "milestone"}], "output_directory": null}}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01XbgWDRLpiyyBLvrw3Ec2kn', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': 'src/field/ensemble_ui/output/logs_agents_tab/milestones.md'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01XbgWDRLpiyyBLvrw3Ec2kn', 'content': '{"success": true, "content": "# Milestone Plan: Backend Logs Tab & Agent Definition Explorer\\n\\n## Project Overview\\nAdd a new \\"Logs & Agents\\" tab to the Ensemble UI with:\\n1. Real-time backend log streaming\\n2. Agent definition file explorer with view/edit capabilities\\n\\n## Technical Decisions Made\\n- **WebSocket for log streaming**: Leverage existing WebSocket infrastructure (already have `/ws/agent-status`)\\n- **React Bootstrap for UI**: Match existing UI framework\\n- **Simple textarea for editing**: No need for Monaco editor initially (per requirements)\\n- **Existing API endpoints**: Leverage `/api/agents`, `/api/agents/{tier}/{name}`, `/api/agents/update`\\n- **Split-pane layout**: Use CSS flexbox for responsive split pane\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Milestone 1: Backend Log Streaming Infrastructure\\n**Objective**: Create WebSocket endpoint and log buffer for real-time log streaming\\n\\n### Deliverables\\n1. Log buffer class with size-limited ring buffer (1000 entries)\\n2. WebSocket endpoint `/ws/logs` for log streaming\\n3. Log filtering by level (INFO, WARNING, ERROR, DEBUG)\\n4. Log filtering by agent_id and request_id\\n5. Structured log entries with timestamp, level, agent_id, request_id, message\\n\\n### Acceptance Criteria\\n- [ ] WebSocket endpoint accepts connections and streams logs\\n- [ ] Log buffer doesn\'t exceed 1000 entries (memory safety)\\n- [ ] Logs include structured metadata (agent_id, request_id, timestamp, level)\\n- [ ] Filtering works on server-side before sending to client\\n- [ ] Existing logging continues to work (no performance degradation)\\n\\n### Dependencies\\n- None (foundational milestone)\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Milestone 2: Frontend Log Viewer Component\\n**Objective**: Create React component to display streamed logs\\n\\n### Deliverables\\n1. `LogStreamPanel.jsx` component\\n2. WebSocket connection to `/ws/logs`\\n3. Auto-scroll with toggle\\n4. Log level filter buttons (INFO, WARNING, ERROR, DEBUG)\\n5. Search filter for agent_id/request_id\\n6. Pause/Resume streaming\\n7. Clear logs button\\n8. Color coding by log level\\n9. Timestamp display (relative/absolute toggle)\\n\\n### Acceptance Criteria\\n- [ ] Component connects to WebSocket and displays logs\\n- [ ] Auto-scroll works and can be toggled\\n- [ ] Filters work correctly (level, search)\\n- [ ] Pause/Resume controls work\\n- [ ] Clear button clears displayed logs\\n- [ ] Color coding matches log levels\\n- [ ] Timestamps are readable\\n\\n### Dependencies\\n- Milestone 1 (backend log streaming)\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Milestone 3: Agent Definition Explorer Component\\n**Objective**: Create tree-view file explorer for agent definitions\\n\\n### Deliverables\\n1. `AgentExplorer.jsx` component\\n2. Tree-view with collapsible directories\\n3. Integration with existing `/api/agents` endpoint\\n4. Directory structure: leadership/, coordinators/, developers/, testers/, designers/\\n5. Click to select agent file\\n6. Visual indicators for selected file\\n\\n### Acceptance Criteria\\n- [ ] Tree displays all agent directories correctly\\n- [ ] Directories can be expanded/collapsed\\n- [ ] Clicking a file selects it\\n- [ ] Visual feedback for selection state\\n- [ ] Icons differentiate files and folders\\n\\n### Dependencies\\n- None (can run in parallel with Milestone 2)\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Milestone 4: Agent Definition Viewer/Editor\\n**Objective**: Create component to view and edit agent definitions\\n\\n### Deliverables\\n1. `AgentDefinitionViewer.jsx` component\\n2. Read-only view mode (default)\\n3. Edit mode with toggle\\n4. Textarea for editing content\\n5. Markdown preview panel\\n6. Save button with confirmation\\n7. Revert functionality (from backup)\\n8. Success/error feedback\\n\\n### Acceptance Criteria\\n- [ ] View mode displays file content\\n- [ ] Edit toggle switches to editable textarea\\n- [ ] Save calls `/api/agents/update` endpoint\\n- [ ] Success message shows backup path\\n- [ ] Revert option works\\n- [ ] Error handling for failed saves\\n\\n### Dependencies\\n- Milestone 3 (explorer provides file selection)\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Milestone 5: Tab Integration & Final Assembly\\n**Objective**: Integrate components into new tab in App.jsx\\n\\n### Deliverables\\n1. Tab navigation component in App.jsx\\n2. \\"Main View\\" tab (existing content)\\n3. \\"Logs & Agents\\" tab (new content)\\n4. Split-pane layout in new tab\\n5. Responsive design\\n6. State management for tab switching\\n\\n### Acceptance Criteria\\n- [ ] Tab navigation works smoothly\\n- [ ] Existing functionality preserved in \\"Main View\\"\\n- [ ] New tab shows logs panel + agent explorer/editor\\n- [ ] Split pane is resizable or has good default split\\n- [ ] UI follows existing dark theme\\n- [ ] All components integrate correctly\\n\\n### Dependencies\\n- Milestones 2, 3, 4 (all components ready)\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Timeline Estimate\\n- Milestone 1: ~2 hours (backend)\\n- Milestone 2: ~3 hours (frontend)\\n- Milestone 3: ~2 hours (frontend)\\n- Milestone 4: ~3 hours (frontend)\\n- Milestone 5: ~2 hours (integration)\\n\\n**Total**: ~12 hours of development work\\n\\n## Risk Assessment\\n1. **Low Risk**: WebSocket infrastructure exists, just adding another endpoint\\n2. **Low Risk**: API endpoints for agents already exist\\n3. **Medium Risk**: Tab integration might need CSS adjustments for layout\\n4. **Low Risk**: React Bootstrap components are well-documented\\n\\n## Success Metrics\\n1. Users can view real-time backend logs without page refresh\\n2. Users can browse all agent definition files in tree structure\\n3. Users can view and edit agent definitions with backup\\n4. Log streaming doesn\'t degrade backend performance\\n5. UI matches existing design patterns\\n"}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01EiGgXMMgAFiFi9pS4CoxAJ', 'name': 'project_tracking', 'input': {'action': 'add_note', 'project_id': 'f09c84d5', 'category': 'milestone', 'note': "Requirements document read successfully. Project involves adding a new 'Logs & Agents' tab to Ensemble UI with real-time backend log streaming and agent definition file explorer. 5 milestones identified with ~12 hours estimated development work."}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01EiGgXMMgAFiFi9pS4CoxAJ', 'content': '{"success": true, "message": "Added note to project"}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01GSzKPqZb5sLpbXSGVRXyFC', 'name': 'write_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements.md', 'content': '# Requirements Document: Logs & Agents Tab Implementation\n\n## Project Vision\nImplement a comprehensive "Logs & Agents" tab for the Ensemble UI that provides real-time backend log monitoring and agent definition file management capabilities. This will enable users to monitor system behavior in real-time and manage agent configurations through a user-friendly interface.\n\n## Core Objectives\n1. **Real-time Log Streaming**: Enable users to view backend logs as they happen\n2. **Agent File Management**: Provide a file explorer for viewing and editing agent definitions\n3. **Seamless Integration**: Add new functionality without disrupting existing UI\n4. **Performance Safety**: Ensure log streaming doesn\'t degrade system performance\n\n## Functional Requirements\n\n### F1: Backend Log Streaming\n- **F1.1**: Create WebSocket endpoint `/ws/logs` for real-time log streaming\n- **F1.2**: Implement log buffer with 1000-entry limit for memory safety\n- **F1.3**: Structure log entries with timestamp, level, agent_id, request_id, message\n- **F1.4**: Support server-side filtering by log level (INFO, WARNING, ERROR, DEBUG)\n- **F1.5**: Support server-side filtering by agent_id and request_id\n- **F1.6**: Maintain existing logging functionality without performance degradation\n\n### F2: Frontend Log Viewer\n- **F2.1**: Create LogStreamPanel component with WebSocket connection\n- **F2.2**: Implement auto-scroll with toggle functionality\n- **F2.3**: Provide log level filter buttons (INFO, WARNING, ERROR, DEBUG)\n- **F2.4**: Include search filter for agent_id/request_id\n- **F2.5**: Support pause/resume streaming controls\n- **F2.6**: Provide clear logs functionality\n- **F2.7**: Implement color coding by log level\n- **F2.8**: Display timestamps with relative/absolute toggle\n\n### F3: Agent Definition Explorer\n- **F3.1**: Create AgentExplorer component with tree-view structure\n- **F3.2**: Display directories: leadership/, coordinators/, developers/, testers/, designers/\n- **F3.3**: Support collapsible/expandable directories\n- **F3.4**: Enable file selection with visual feedback\n- **F3.5**: Use existing `/api/agents` endpoint for data\n- **F3.6**: Differentiate files and folders with appropriate icons\n\n### F4: Agent Definition Editor\n- **F4.1**: Create AgentDefinitionViewer component with read-only default view\n- **F4.2**: Implement edit mode toggle with textarea editing\n- **F4.3**: Provide markdown preview panel\n- **F4.4**: Integrate with existing `/api/agents/update` endpoint for saving\n- **F4.5**: Implement automatic backup functionality\n- **F4.6**: Provide revert functionality using backups\n- **F4.7**: Display success/error feedback for save operations\n\n### F5: Tab Integration\n- **F5.1**: Add tab navigation to App.jsx with "Main View" and "Logs & Agents" tabs\n- **F5.2**: Preserve all existing functionality in "Main View" tab\n- **F5.3**: Implement split-pane layout in "Logs & Agents" tab\n- **F5.4**: Ensure responsive design across screen sizes\n- **F5.5**: Maintain consistent dark theme styling\n\n## Non-Functional Requirements\n\n### NF1: Performance\n- Log streaming must not degrade backend performance\n- WebSocket connections should be efficiently managed\n- Log buffer must not exceed memory constraints (1000 entries)\n\n### NF2: Usability\n- UI must follow existing design patterns and dark theme\n- Components must be responsive across different screen sizes\n- Interface should be intuitive for developers and administrators\n\n### NF3: Reliability\n- WebSocket connections should handle disconnections gracefully\n- File editing should include backup/recovery mechanisms\n- Error states should be clearly communicated to users\n\n### NF4: Maintainability\n- Code should follow existing project conventions\n- Components should be modular and reusable\n- TDD methodology must be followed (tests before implementation)\n\n## Technical Constraints\n- Must use existing WebSocket infrastructure (building on `/ws/agent-status`)\n- Must use React Bootstrap for UI consistency\n- Must integrate with existing API endpoints (`/api/agents`, `/api/agents/{tier}/{name}`, `/api/agents/update`)\n- Must use simple textarea for editing (no Monaco editor requirement)\n- Must use CSS flexbox for split-pane layout\n\n## Success Criteria\n1. Users can view real-time backend logs without page refresh\n2. Log streaming includes filtering by level and search terms\n3. Users can browse agent definition files in intuitive tree structure\n4. Users can view and edit agent definitions with automatic backup\n5. Tab integration preserves existing functionality\n6. System performance remains stable under normal log volume\n7. All tests pass (following TDD methodology)\n8. UI maintains consistency with existing design\n\n## Out of Scope\n- Advanced log analysis or aggregation features\n- Complex code editing features (syntax highlighting, IntelliSense)\n- User authentication/authorization for file editing\n- Log persistence to database\n- Advanced layout customization options\n\n## Dependencies\n- Existing WebSocket infrastructure (`/ws/agent-status`)\n- Existing agent API endpoints\n- React Bootstrap framework\n- Current dark theme CSS\n\n## Assumptions Made\n- Standard log volumes won\'t exceed buffer capacity under normal operation\n- Users have appropriate permissions for file system access\n- Existing API endpoints provide sufficient data for agent management\n- WebSocket infrastructure can handle additional concurrent connections\n- Current UI framework (React Bootstrap) is sufficient for new components\n\n## Testing Requirements\nFollowing TDD methodology:\n1. Unit tests for all React components\n2. Integration tests for WebSocket connections\n3. API integration tests for agent management\n4. End-to-end tests for complete user workflows\n5. Performance tests for log streaming under load'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01GSzKPqZb5sLpbXSGVRXyFC', 'content': '{"success": true, "message": "File written successfully to /Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements.md (backup: /Users/mattbillock/.ensemble/backups/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements_20260116_224231.md)", "backup_path": "/Users/mattbillock/.ensemble/backups/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements_20260116_224231.md", "was_overwrite": true}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01XzYwAZ6JBsk96jVGakTRDU', 'name': 'project_tracking', 'input': {'action': 'add_note', 'project_id': 'f09c84d5', 'category': 'milestone', 'note': 'Requirements document completed and written to /Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements.md. Ready to delegate to Development Manager for implementation.'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', '