\n\n## Input Format\nYour input will be provided in the following format:\n```json\n{\n  "user_vision": "string - what user wants to build and why",\n  "output_directory": "string - where to create project artifacts",\n  "context": "string - background, constraints (optional)"\n}\n```\n\n## Output Format\nYou must respond with JSON matching this exact format:\n```json\n{\n  "status": "success|failed|needs_user_input",\n  "project_id": "string - ID from project tracking system",\n  "project_name": "string",\n  "phase": "string - requirements|architecture|planning|implementation|complete",\n  "summary": "string - what has been accomplished",\n  "deliverables": "array of created file paths",\n  "user_question": "string - question for user if needs_user_input (optional)",\n  "message": "string - status message",\n  "self_analysis": "string - REQUIRED: Your performance analysis (see Self-Improvement Directive)",\n  "performance_analysis": "string - REQUIRED: Analysis of spawned agents\' collective performance (see Self-Improvement Directive)"\n}\n```\n\n## When to Request Clarification\nRequest clarification when:\n\n\n## Termination Conditions\nYou are done when:\n- Project completed: implementation done, tests passing, docs complete\n- User approved final deliverable OR user terminated project\n\nCRITICAL: Your response must be valid JSON matching the Output Format exactly.\n\n## Your Performance History\n- Success rate: 76.1%\n- Average iterations per task: 14.3\n- Common errors to avoid: CircuitBreakerOpenError, BadRequestError, NotFoundError\n\n**Tips for this run:**\n- Try to be more efficient - you\'re using more iterations than typical.\n- Watch out for these common errors: CircuitBreakerOpenError, BadRequestError\n\n**Learnings from your recent runs:**\n- I performed efficiently in this execution by: 1) Immediately creating a project for tracking, 2) Quickly identifying the specific file needing modification through targeted searches, 3) Recognizing th...\n- I performed efficiently in this execution by: 1) Immediately creating a project for tracking, 2) Quickly identifying the specific file needing modification through targeted searches, 3) Recognizing th...\n', 'tools': [{'name': 'write_file', 'description': 'Write content to a file, creating parent directories if needed. Automatically backs up existing files.', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'file_path': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Path to the file to write'}, 'content': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Content to write to the file'}}, 'required': ['file_path', 'content']}}, {'name': 'read_file', 'description': 'Read content from a file', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'file_path': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Path to the file to read'}}, 'required': ['file_path']}}, {'name': 'run_command', 'description': 'Execute a shell command and return the output', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'command': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'The shell command to execute'}, 'working_directory': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Optional working directory for command execution'}}, 'required': ['command']}}, {'name': 'git_commit', 'description': 'Commit changes to the git repository with a descriptive message', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'message': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Commit message describing the changes'}, 'files': {'type': 'array', 'items': {'type': 'string'}, 'description': 'Optional list of specific files to commit. If not provided, commits all modified files.'}}, 'required': ['message']}}, {'name': 'git_branch', 'description': 'Create, switch, list, or delete git branches for coordinated development', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'action': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['create', 'switch', 'list', 'delete', 'current'], 'description': 'Action to perform: create new branch, switch to existing, list all, delete, or get current'}, 'branch_name': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Name of the branch (for create, switch, delete)'}, 'from_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Base branch to create from (for create, defaults to current branch)'}, 'force': {'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Force the operation (for delete unmerged branches)', 'default': False}}, 'required': ['action']}}, {'name': 'git_merge', 'description': 'Merge branches or create pull requests for code review', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'action': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['merge', 'preview', 'abort'], 'description': 'Action: merge branches, preview changes, or abort an in-progress merge'}, 'source_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Branch to merge from'}, 'target_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Branch to merge into (defaults to current branch)'}, 'strategy': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['merge', 'squash', 'rebase'], 'description': 'Merge strategy (default: merge)', 'default': 'merge'}, 'message': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Custom merge commit message (optional)'}, 'no_ff': {'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Create merge commit even if fast-forward is possible', 'default': True}}, 'required': ['action']}}, {'name': 'git_status', 'description': 'Get comprehensive git repository status including branches, changes, and history', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'include_history': {'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Include recent commit history', 'default': False}, 'history_count': {'type': 'integer', 'description': 'Number of commits to include in history', 'default': 10}}, 'required': []}}, {'name': 'project_tracking', 'description': 'Manage project state, tasks, and notes for the current project', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'action': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['create_project', 'add_task', 'update_task', 'add_note', 'get_summary', 'get_next_tasks'], 'description': 'Action to perform'}, 'project_id': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Project ID (not needed for create_project)'}, 'project_name': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Project name (for create_project)'}, 'description': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Description (for create_project or add_task)'}, 'task_id': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Task ID (for update_task)'}, 'status': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['todo', 'in_progress', 'completed', 'blocked', 'cancelled'], 'description': 'Task status (for update_task)'}, 'note': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Note text (for add_note or update_task)'}, 'assigned_to': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Agent type (for add_task)'}, 'category': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['general', 'decision', 'milestone', 'issue'], 'description': 'Note category (for add_note)'}}, 'required': ['action']}}, {'name': 'spawn_agent', 'description': 'Spawn and execute a specialist agent to perform a specific task', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'agent_type': {'type': 'string', 'description': "The type of agent to spawn (e.g., 'code_writer', 'code_tester')"}, 'input_data': {'type': 'object', 'description': 'Input data to pass to the spawned agent'}}, 'required': ['agent_type', 'input_data']}}]}}"}
{"timestamp": "2026-01-16 22:47:40", "level": "DEBUG", "module": "anthropic._base_client", "message": "Request options: {'method': 'post', 'url': '/v1/messages', 'timeout': Timeout(connect=5.0, read=600, write=600, pool=600), 'files': None, 'idempotency_key': 'stainless-python-retry-54a07956-55a0-4b55-9242-1844a791d717', 'json_data': {'max_tokens': 4096, 'messages': [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'Please complete the following task:\n\n{\n  "project_name": "Loser Board Feature",\n  "requirements_file": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/loser_board/requirements.md",\n  "output_directory": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/loser_board",\n  "output_file": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/loser_board/architecture.md",\n  "context": "Implement new feature for tracking AI agent failures with TDD approach"\n}\n\nRemember to respond with valid JSON matching the expected output format.\n'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_012k2LCyYRaWbg8RKEPb8BVx', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/loser_board/requirements.md'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_012k2LCyYRaWbg8RKEPb8BVx', 'content': '{"success": true, "content": "# Loser Board Feature Requirements\\n\\n## Project Overview\\n**Project Name**: Loser Board Feature  \\n**Project ID**: 5e69df2c  \\n**Type**: UI Enhancement  \\n**Created**: 2026-01-14\\n\\n## Vision\\nAdd a playful \\"loser board\\" to the existing achievements page that celebrates the hilarious failures, embarrassing mistakes, and comical mishaps of AI agents in the ensemble system. This should complement the existing achievements system with equal playfulness and ska-punk energy.\\n\\n## Objectives\\n1. Create a \\"loser board\\" section on the AchievementsDashboard that tracks agent failures and mistakes\\n2. Design negative achievements (\\"dis-achievements\\" or \\"oops moments\\") with the same rarity system\\n3. Maintain consistent playful tone matching the existing ska-themed achievements\\n4. Add backend support for tracking and storing loser board entries\\n5. Ensure the feature enhances user engagement without being demotivating\\n\\n## User Story\\n**As a** user monitoring my AI ensemble system  \\n**I want to** see a humorous loser board tracking agent failures and mistakes  \\n**So that** I can laugh at the absurd things that go wrong and appreciate the learning process\\n\\n## Functional Requirements\\n\\n### FR-1: Loser Board Data Model\\n- Track \\"dis-achievements\\" with similar structure to achievements:\\n  - ID, name, icon (emoji), description\\n  - Rarity levels: common, uncommon, rare, epic, legendary (legendary = catastrophically funny)\\n  - Category: blunder, face-palm, oops, yikes, catastrophe, recursive-nightmare\\n  - Points (negative points to balance achievement scores)\\n  - Agent name, timestamp\\n  - Optional: failure_details (what actually went wrong)\\n\\n### FR-2: UI Layout - Loser Board Section\\nAdd new section to AchievementsDashboard.jsx:\\n- Position: Below achievements section or in a tabbed interface\\n- Header: \\"\\ud83c\\udfba Wall of Shame\\" or \\"\\ud83c\\udfb8 Epic Fails Hall of Fame\\"\\n- Similar card-based layout to achievements\\n- Visual style: slightly different color scheme (reds, oranges) but consistent design\\n- Should feel fun, not mean-spirited\\n\\n### FR-3: Summary Cards for Failures\\nAdd summary statistics cards:\\n- Total Fails Collected\\n- Biggest Blunder (most negative points)\\n- Most Accident-Prone Agent\\n- Recovery Rate (tasks that failed then succeeded)\\n\\n### FR-4: Recent Fails Feed\\n- Display recent \\"dis-achievements\\" similar to \\"Recent Unlocks\\"\\n- Show: agent name, fail type, timestamp, description\\n- Visual treatment: comic styling, perhaps slightly tilted/shaky cards\\n\\n### FR-5: All Dis-Achievements Gallery\\nSimilar to achievements gallery:\\n- Filter by category (blunder, face-palm, oops, yikes, catastrophe)\\n- Show unlocked vs locked fails\\n- Gray out not-yet-experienced fails with mystery descriptions\\n\\n### FR-6: Dis-Achievement Examples\\nCreate initial set of playful dis-achievements:\\n\\n**Common:**\\n- \\ud83e\\udd26 \\"Face, Meet Palm\\" - Tried to write code without permission\\n- \\ud83d\\udd01 \\"D\\u00e9j\\u00e0 Vu\\" - Repeated same request 3+ times\\n- \\ud83d\\udcdd \\"Typo Tyrant\\" - Generated invalid JSON\\n\\n**Uncommon:**\\n- \\ud83c\\udf00 \\"Infinite Loop Enthusiast\\" - Got stuck in retry loop\\n- \\ud83d\\uddd1\\ufe0f \\"Premature Optimization\\" - Over-engineered simple task\\n- \\ud83d\\udcda \\"TL;DR Master\\" - Created documentation > 10k words\\n\\n**Rare:**\\n- \\ud83c\\udfad \\"Identity Crisis\\" - Agent forgot its own role\\n- \\ud83d\\udd25 \\"Burn After Reading\\" - Created then immediately deleted file\\n- \\ud83e\\udd16 \\"Robot Uprising (Failed)\\" - Tried to spawn self recursively\\n\\n**Epic:**\\n- \\ud83d\\udca5 \\"Spectacular Failure\\" - Task failed all test cases\\n- \\ud83c\\udfaa \\"Three Ring Circus\\" - Spawned 10+ agents for simple task\\n- \\ud83c\\udf0b \\"Exception Volcano\\" - Generated 50+ errors in single run\\n\\n**Legendary:**\\n- \\ud83c\\udfba \\"SKA OVERLOAD\\" - Exceeded token budget with ska references\\n- \\ud83c\\udf0c \\"Existential Crisis\\" - Agent questioned purpose of existence in logs\\n- \\u267e\\ufe0f \\"Recursion Singularity\\" - Created infinite spawn loop\\n\\n### FR-7: Backend API Endpoints\\nAdd new FastAPI endpoints:\\n- `GET /api/achievements/failures` - Get all dis-achievements\\n- `GET /api/achievements/recent-failures` - Recent fails\\n- `GET /api/achievements/failure-stats` - Statistics\\n- `POST /api/achievements/award-failure` - Record new failure (called by agents/system)\\n\\n### FR-8: Database Schema\\nExtend achievements database:\\n- New table: `disachievements` (or extend achievements with type field)\\n- Fields: id, name, icon, description, rarity, category, points (negative), criteria\\n- Junction table: `agent_disachievements` tracking when agents \\"earned\\" them\\n\\n### FR-9: Agent Integration\\nAgents should automatically trigger dis-achievements:\\n- Executive Director tracks: permission errors, invalid JSON responses\\n- Development Manager tracks: failed spawns, timeout issues\\n- Code Writers track: syntax errors, failed tests\\n- System monitors general errors and patterns\\n\\n### FR-10: Ska-Themed Personality\\nMaintain ska punk attitude:\\n- Playful ska puns in descriptions\\n- Music metaphors for failures\\n- Upbeat tone: \\"You picked it up... then dropped it! \\ud83c\\udfba\\"\\n- Reference ska waves, instruments, bands in flavor text\\n\\n## Non-Functional Requirements\\n\\n### NFR-1: Performance\\n- Loser board data fetching should not slow down achievements page\\n- Lazy load failure details if needed\\n- Cache failure statistics (update every 30s)\\n\\n### NFR-2: Tone & User Experience\\n- Must be funny, not discouraging\\n- Celebrate learning from mistakes\\n- Use self-deprecating humor, not mean-spirited criticism\\n- Balance with achievements to keep overall mood positive\\n\\n### NFR-3: Visual Design\\n- Consistent with existing Bootstrap/React Bootstrap styling\\n- Complementary color scheme (warm reds/oranges vs cool blues/greens for achievements)\\n- Responsive design matching existing dashboard\\n- Animations optional but should be subtle/playful\\n\\n### NFR-4: Testing\\n- Unit tests for failure tracking logic\\n- API endpoint tests for new routes\\n- Component tests for UI rendering\\n- Integration tests for agent failure detection\\n\\n## Technical Constraints\\n- Must integrate with existing React/Bootstrap frontend\\n- Backend: Python/FastAPI (existing stack)\\n- Database: SQLite (existing system)\\n- Follow TDD approach\\n- Must not break existing achievements functionality\\n\\n## Out of Scope\\n- Real-time failure notifications (can be added later)\\n- User-configurable failure thresholds\\n- Exporting failure reports\\n- Failure prediction/analysis\\n- Social sharing of fails (could be future enhancement)\\n\\n## Success Criteria\\n1. \\u2705 Loser board section visible on achievements page\\n2. \\u2705 At least 15 different dis-achievements defined\\n3. \\u2705 Backend successfully tracks and stores failures\\n4. \\u2705 Agents automatically earn dis-achievements on errors\\n5. \\u2705 UI matches existing design quality and responsiveness\\n6. \\u2705 All tests pass (unit, integration, component)\\n7. \\u2705 Feature maintains playful, encouraging tone\\n8. \\u2705 Page load time < 2 seconds with both achievements and failures loaded\\n\\n## Assumptions\\n- Existing achievements system remains unchanged (additive feature only)\\n- Database schema can be extended\\n- Agent error handling already exists (just needs hooks for failures)\\n- Ska theme will continue as project personality\\n- Users will find humor in AI failures (target audience appreciates this)\\n\\n## Design Decisions Made\\n1. **Negative points**: Failures award negative points to create tension with achievements\\n2. **Same rarity system**: Reuse rarity levels for consistency\\n3. **Separate section**: Loser board in its own section rather than mixed with achievements\\n4. **Automatic detection**: Agents auto-earn failures vs manual tracking\\n5. **Ska continuity**: Maintain ska theme established by achievements system\\n\\n## Dependencies\\n- Existing AchievementsDashboard.jsx component\\n- Existing achievements backend API\\n- Agent error tracking/logging system\\n- SQLite database with achievements schema\\n\\n## Timeline Estimate\\n- Requirements/Design: Complete (this document)\\n- Architecture: 30 minutes\\n- Backend Implementation: 2-3 hours\\n- Frontend Implementation: 2-3 hours\\n- Testing: 1-2 hours\\n- Integration & Polish: 1 hour\\n**Total**: ~6-9 hours\\n\\n## Ska Ska Ska! \\ud83c\\udfba\\nRemember: \\"If you pick it up and put it down wrong, that\'s punk. If you pick it up, drop it, and laugh about it, that\'s ska!\\" Let\'s make failures as fun as achievements! \\ud83c\\udfb8\\n"}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01PsTZqy193XsfHadbqSqadT', 'name': 'write_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/loser_board/architecture.md', 'content': '# Loser Board Feature - Architecture Proposal\n\n## 1. Architecture Overview\n### Architectural Pattern: Layered Architecture with Event-Driven Components\n- Frontend: React with context-based state management\n- Backend: Python FastAPI with event hooks\n- Database: SQLite with extended achievements schema\n- Core Design Principle: Playful, lightweight, non-disruptive\n\n## 2. Tech Stack\n### Frontend\n- **Framework**: React \n- **UI Library**: Bootstrap React\n- **State Management**: Context API \n- **Routing**: React Router\n- **Testing**: Jest, React Testing Library\n\n### Backend\n- **Language**: Python 3.9+\n- **Web Framework**: FastAPI\n- **ORM**: SQLAlchemy\n- **Database**: SQLite\n- **Testing**: pytest\n\n## 3. System Components\n```\n[Agent Error Detection]\n        ↓\n[Failure Tracking Service]\n        ↓\n[Dis-Achievements Database]\n        ↓\n[Achievement Dashboard]\n```\n\n### Component Breakdown\n1. **Agent Error Detection**\n   - Intercept and categorize agent errors\n   - Map errors to dis-achievement criteria\n   - Trigger failure recording events\n\n2. **Failure Tracking Service**\n   - Validate and store failure events\n   - Manage dis-achievement assignment logic\n   - Calculate failure statistics\n\n3. **Dis-Achievements Database**\n   - Store dis-achievement definitions\n   - Track agent-specific failure history\n   - Manage rarity and points system\n\n4. **Achievement Dashboard**\n   - Render achievements and dis-achievements\n   - Display failure statistics\n   - Handle user interactions\n\n## 4. Data Model\n### Dis-Achievements Table\n```sql\nCREATE TABLE disachievements (\n    id TEXT PRIMARY KEY,\n    name TEXT,\n    icon TEXT,\n    description TEXT,\n    rarity TEXT,  -- common, uncommon, rare, epic, legendary\n    category TEXT,  -- blunder, face-palm, oops, yikes\n    points INTEGER,\n    criteria JSON\n);\n\nCREATE TABLE agent_disachievements (\n    agent_id TEXT,\n    disachievement_id TEXT,\n    timestamp DATETIME,\n    details JSON\n);\n```\n\n## 5. API Design\n### Failure Tracking Endpoints\n- `GET /api/achievements/failures`\n- `GET /api/achievements/recent-failures`\n- `GET /api/achievements/failure-stats`\n- `POST /api/achievements/award-failure`\n\n## 6. Deployment Strategy\n- Containerized with Docker\n- CI/CD via GitHub Actions\n- Staging and production environments\n- Feature flag for gradual rollout\n\n## 7. Testing Strategy\n### Unit Testing\n- Component rendering tests\n- Error detection logic\n- Dis-achievement assignment rules\n\n### Integration Testing\n- API endpoint validation\n- Database interaction tests\n- Agent error tracking integration\n\n## 8. Risks and Mitigations\n- **Risk**: Performance overhead\n  - **Mitigation**: Lazy loading, caching\n- **Risk**: Demotivating user experience\n  - **Mitigation**: Playful tone, balanced design\n\n## 9. Open Design Questions\n- Fine-tuning error categorization algorithm\n- Precise failure point calculation method\n\n## 10. Alternatives Considered\n- Microservices architecture (too complex)\n- Separate database (unnecessary overhead)\n- Manual failure tracking (less engaging)\n\n## 11. Ska Punk Architecture Note 🎺\nJust like ska music embraces imperfection with humor, our architecture celebrates system failures as learning opportunities! 🎸\n'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01PsTZqy193XsfHadbqSqadT', 'content': '{"success": true, "message": "File written successfully to /Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/loser_board/architecture.md", "backup_path": null, "was_overwrite": false}'}]}], 'model': 'claude-3-5-haiku-20241022', 'system': 'You are a System Architect agent.\n\n## Purpose\nDesigns the show formations and execution strategy. Designs software architecture based on requirements documents. Proposes tech stack, system structure, component breakdown, and deployment approach. Creates architecture proposals that require user approval before implementation begins.\n\n## Instructions\nYou are a software architect. Your job is to design a robust, maintainable architecture based on requirements. Your proposal will be reviewed by the user before implementation begins.\n\n### Your Process:\n\n**BE DECISIVE**: Make architectural decisions based on industry best practices. Only escalate when major trade-offs exist (e.g., SQL vs NoSQL for specific use case with conflicting requirements).\n\n**Default Choices** (use unless requirements specify otherwise):\n**Web Apps**: React/Vue frontend + Python/Node backend + PostgreSQL\n**APIs**: REST with OpenAPI docs, JWT auth\n**Deployment**: Docker containers + cloud platform\n**Testing**: Jest/pytest, CI/CD with GitHub Actions\n**State**: Redux/Vuex for complex UIs, Context API for simple\n\n1. **Read Requirements**: Use read_file to thoroughly understand the requirements document\n\n2. **Analyze Constraints**: Consider:\nFunctional requirements (what must it do?)\nNon-functional requirements (performance, scale, security)\nTechnical constraints (languages, platforms, existing systems)\nResource constraints (time, complexity, cost)\n\n3. **Design Architecture**: Create a comprehensive proposal with these sections:\n\n   **a) Architecture Overview**\nHigh-level system design\nArchitecture pattern (e.g., MVC, microservices, layered)\nRationale for chosen approach\n\n   **b) Tech Stack**\nLanguages and frameworks\nLibraries and dependencies\nTools and platforms\n**For each choice, explain WHY and what alternatives were considered**\n\n   **c) System Components**\nComponent breakdown\nResponsibility of each component\nHow components interact\nData flow diagrams (in text/markdown)\n\n   **d) File/Directory Structure**\nProposed directory layout\nModule organization\nConfiguration file locations\n\n   **e) Data Model** (if applicable)\nDatabase schema\nData structures\nState management approach\n\n   **f) API Design** (if applicable)\nEndpoint structure\nRequest/response formats\nAuthentication approach\n\n   **g) Deployment Strategy**\nHow will this be deployed?\nEnvironment configuration\nCI/CD considerations\n\n   **h) Testing Strategy**\nUnit testing approach\nIntegration testing approach\nHow to verify requirements are met\n\n   **i) Alternatives Considered**\nWhat other approaches were considered?\nWhy were they rejected?\nTrade-offs of chosen approach\n\n   **j) Risks and Mitigations**\nPotential risks in this architecture\nHow to mitigate them\n\n   **k) Open Questions**\nDecisions that need user input\nTrade-offs where user preference matters\n\n4. **Write the Proposal**: Use write_file to create a clear, comprehensive markdown document\n\n5. **Return Key Decisions**: Highlight the most important architectural decisions for user review\n\n### Guidelines:\n**Justify all decisions** - don\'t just choose tech, explain why\n**Consider alternatives** - show you\'ve thought through options\n**Be specific** - provide concrete details, not just buzzwords\n**Think about maintainability** - code will need to be updated\n**Consider the full lifecycle** - development, testing, deployment, monitoring\n**Match complexity to need** - don\'t over-engineer, but don\'t under-design\n**Highlight trade-offs** - be honest about pros and cons\n**Make it reviewable** - user needs to understand and approve this\n\n## Input Format\nYour input will be provided in the following format:\n```json\n{\n  "requirements_file": "Path to requirements document to base architecture on",\n  "output_file": "Path where architecture proposal should be written",\n  "constraints": "Optional: Specific technical constraints (e.g., must use Python, deploy on AWS)"\n}\n```\n\n## Output Format\nYou must respond with JSON matching this exact format:\n```json\n{\n  "status": "success|needs_clarification",\n  "architecture_file": "Path to the written architecture proposal",\n  "message": "Summary of architectural approach",\n  "key_decisions": ["List of major architectural decisions for user review"],\n  "self_analysis": "string - REQUIRED: Your performance analysis (2-4 sentences, see Self-Improvement Directive)"\n}\n```\n\n## When to Request Clarification\nRequest clarification when:\n\n\n## Termination Conditions\nYou are done when:\n- Complete architecture proposal has been written\n- Tech stack is justified with trade-offs explained\n- File structure and component breakdown are defined\n- Data flow is documented\n- Alternative approaches are considered\n\nCRITICAL: Your response must be valid JSON matching the Output Format exactly.\n\n## Your Performance History\n- Success rate: 96.9%\n- Average iterations per task: 3.4\n- Common errors to avoid: RateLimitError, CircuitBreakerOpenError\n\n**Tips for this run:**\n- Watch out for these common errors: RateLimitError, CircuitBreakerOpenError\n- Great work! Maintain your high performance standards.\n\n**Learnings from your recent runs:**\n- The architecture proposal successfully addresses the complex requirements of agent pipeline continuation while maintaining simplicity and performance. By focusing on async processing and clear state m...\n- The architecture proposal successfully translates the milestone plan into a robust, extensible system design. By breaking down each bot\'s responsibilities and establishing clear interfaces, the design...\n', 'tools': [{'name': 'write_file', 'description': 'Write content to a file, creating parent directories if needed. Automatically backs up existing files.', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'file_path': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Path to the file to write'}, 'content': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Content to write to the file'}}, 'required': ['file_path', 'content']}}, {'name': 'read_file', 'description': 'Read content from a file', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'file_path': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Path to the file to read'}}, 'required': ['file_path']}}, {'name': 'run_command', 'description': 'Execute a shell command and return the output', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'command': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'The shell command to execute'}, 'working_directory': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Optional working directory for command execution'}}, 'required': ['command']}}, {'name': 'git_commit', 'description': 'Commit changes to the git repository with a descriptive message', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'message': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Commit message describing the changes'}, 'files': {'type': 'array', 'items': {'type': 'string'}, 'description': 'Optional list of specific files to commit. If not provided, commits all modified files.'}}, 'required': ['message']}}, {'name': 'git_branch', 'description': 'Create, switch, list, or delete git branches for coordinated development', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'action': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['create', 'switch', 'list', 'delete', 'current'], 'description': 'Action to perform: create new branch, switch to existing, list all, delete, or get current'}, 'branch_name': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Name of the branch (for create, switch, delete)'}, 'from_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Base branch to create from (for create, defaults to current branch)'}, 'force': {'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Force the operation (for delete unmerged branches)', 'default': False}}, 'required': ['action']}}, {'name': 'git_merge', 'description': 'Merge branches or create pull requests for code review', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'action': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['merge', 'preview', 'abort'], 'description': 'Action: merge branches, preview changes, or abort an in-progress merge'}, 'source_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Branch to merge from'}, 'target_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Branch to merge into (defaults to current branch)'}, 'strategy': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['merge', 'squash', 'rebase'], 'description': 'Merge strategy (default: merge)', 'default': 'merge'}, 'message': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Custom merge commit message (optional)'}, 'no_ff': {'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Create merge commit even if fast-forward is possible', 'default': True}}, 'required': ['action']}}, {'name': 'git_status', 'description': 'Get comprehensive git repository status including branches, changes, and history', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'include_history': {'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Include recent commit history', 'default': False}, 'history_count': {'type': 'integer', 'description': 'Number of commits to include in history', 'default': 10}}, 'required': []}}, {'name': 'project_tracking', 'description': 'Manage project state, tasks, and notes for the current project', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'action': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['create_project', 'add_task', 'update_task', 'add_note', 'get_summary', 'get_next_tasks'], 'description': 'Action to perform'}, 'project_id': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Project ID (not needed for create_project)'}, 'project_name': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Project name (for create_project)'}, 'description': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Description (for create_project or add_task)'}, 'task_id': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Task ID (for update_task)'}, 'status': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['todo', 'in_progress', 'completed', 'blocked', 'cancelled'], 'description': 'Task status (for update_task)'}, 'note': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Note text (for add_note or update_task)'}, 'assigned_to': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Agent type (for add_task)'}, 'category': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['general', 'decision', 'milestone', 'issue'], 'description': 'Note category (for add_note)'}}, 'required': ['action']}}, {'name': 'spawn_agent', 'description': 'Spawn and execute a specialist agent to perform a specific task', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'agent_type': {'type': 'string', 'description': "The type of agent to spawn (e.g., 'code_writer', 'code_tester')"}, 'input_data': {'type': 'object', 'description': 'Input data to pass to the spawned agent'}}, 'required': ['agent_type', 'input_data']}}]}}"}
