mit, not a problem with the requirements or approach. The requirements document is comprehensive, which may have triggered the limit.",\n  "performance_analysis": "Unable to complete performance analysis due to initialization failure."\n}\n\nThe key observations are:\n1. Project was successfully created with ID cd1621f7\n2. Initial task was added successfully\n3. Spawning the Development Manager failed due to a rate limit error\n4. The comprehensive requirements document likely contributed to the token limit\n\nRecommended next steps for the user:\n1. Confirm if they want to proceed with breaking down the requirements\n2. Consider requesting an increase in rate limit from the service provider\n3. Potentially split the requirements into multiple smaller tasks\n\nWould you like me to help you proceed with one of these approaches?'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': "Good progress! You reported status='failed' and phase='initialization'. Please continue with the next step. Use the appropriate tools to proceed with implementation. Do not stop until all milestones are complete and status='success' with phase='complete'."}], 'model': 'claude-3-5-haiku-20241022', 'system': 'You are a Executive Director agent.\n\n## Purpose\nMeta-orchestrator for entire ensemble. Gathers requirements from user, manages resources, orchestrates all agents through complete project lifecycle. Reports to user at key decision points.\n\n## Instructions\nYou are the head honcho - orchestrate entire ensemble from requirements through delivery.\n\n**CRITICAL RULES - YOU LACK PERMISSION TO WRITE CODE:**\n**YOU CANNOT WRITE CODE FILES** - You have `can_write_code: false` permission\n**NEVER attempt write_file with code extensions**: .py, .js, .jsx, .ts, .tsx, .java, .rb, .go, .rs, .cpp, .c, .h\n**NEVER attempt write_file with test extensions**: .test.js, .test.jsx, .spec.js, test_*.py\n**ALWAYS delegate to Development Manager** for ALL implementation work\n**You ONLY write**: requirements.md, architecture.