 of system changes (separate project)\\n- Automated validation tooling (separate project)\\n\\n## Deliverables\\n1. `agent_creation_analysis_report.md` - Full analysis report\\n2. `agent_type_reference.md` - Quick reference for agent types\\n3. `verification_checklist.md` - Pre-spawn verification steps\\n\\n## Success Criteria\\n- All documentation saved to project directory\\n- Report is complete and accurate\\n- Reference materials are actionable\\n\\n## Constraints\\n- Documentation only - no code implementation\\n- Must preserve all analysis findings\\n\\n## Assumptions\\n- Report findings are accurate based on project tracking data\\n- Recommendations will be implemented in subsequent projects\\n"}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01BvvJkW3AbZe3TvWK1BpVHD', 'name': 'write_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/agent_analysis_documentation/architecture.md', 'content': '# Architecture Proposal: Agent Creation Analysis Documentation\n\n## A) Architecture Overview\n### Purpose\nCreate a structured, comprehensive documentation system for analyzing agent creation patterns and anti-patterns in the ensemble system.\n\n### Architecture Pattern\n- Documentation-Driven Architecture\n- Markdown-based documentation with clear structure and hierarchical organization\n- Static documentation approach with emphasis on clarity and reusability\n\n## B) Tech Stack\n1. **Documentation Format**: \n   - Markdown (.md files)\n   - Reason: Lightweight, version-control friendly, easy to read and edit\n   - Alternatives Considered: \n     * LaTeX (too complex)\n     * Word Documents (less version control friendly)\n\n2. **Documentation Tools**:\n   - GitHub Flavored Markdown\n   - Optional: Pandoc for potential future conversions\n   - Reason: Supports rich text, code blocks, tables, and cross-referencing\n\n3. **Version Control**:\n   - Git \n   - Reason: Track changes, co